Set CARGO_HOME inside the WheelBuild action sandbox.

pycross_wheel_build's action env is the C++ toolchain vars plus
--action_env entries; nothing provides CARGO_HOME. When an sdist's
PEP 517 backend invokes cargo (setuptools-rust, maturin), cargo
resolves $HOME/.cargo — which is unwritable inside Bazel's sandbox
(failing the build) and non-hermetic outside it (registry/cache state
leaks between builds). Default CARGO_HOME to `.cargo`, relative to the
action's working directory, so cargo state stays inside the sandbox
and is discarded with it.

No package in mongodb's current uv.lock builds Rust from sdist (the
one Rust-heavy dep, cryptography, uses prebuilt wheels for the
platforms PyPI doesn't cover), so this is insurance for the first dep
that does — carried over from the equivalent tweak mongodb applied to
rules_poetry's deterministic_env() in the pre-uv setup.

Applied via `single_version_override(patches=...)` on rules_pycross in
//MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to jvolkman/rules_pycross.

--- a/pycross/private/wheel_build.bzl	2026-07-24 10:35:15
+++ b/pycross/private/wheel_build.bzl	2026-07-24 10:35:31
@@ -348,6 +348,15 @@
     env = dict(cc_vars)
     env.update(ctx.configuration.default_shell_env)
 
+    # Keep Rust-backed sdist builds (cargo, invoked by build backends like
+    # setuptools-rust / maturin) inside the action's writable sandbox.
+    # Without CARGO_HOME, cargo resolves $HOME/.cargo — unwritable in the
+    # sandbox and non-hermetic outside it. The relative path lands under the
+    # action's working directory (the execroot) and is discarded with the
+    # sandbox. Carried over from the equivalent tweak mongodb applied to
+    # rules_poetry's deterministic_env().
+    env.setdefault("CARGO_HOME", ".cargo")
+
     ctx.actions.run(
         inputs = inputs,
         outputs = [pycross_wheel_info.wheel_file, pycross_wheel_info.name_file],
